$folder — load all files from a directory into the bundle

SUMMARY
  Reads every file in a directory (non-recursive, sorted by name) and appends
  links to the appropriate arrays based on file extension — same mapping as $file.

SYNTAX
  $folder('path/to/dir')
  $folder('path/to/dir', '*.py')
  $folder('path/to/dir', source_path=True)
  $folder('test_data', '*.mp4', subfolders=True)
  $folder(path='test_data/videos', pattern='*.wav')

INPUT
  prompts, texts, images, sounds, videos, files — unchanged (copied through)

OUTPUT
  Appends one link per file, routed by extension:
    .mp3, .wav  → sounds[]
    .png, .jpg, .jpeg, .webp → images[]
    .mp4        → videos[]
    .txt, .ass  → texts[]
    other       → files[]

  Full mapping: externals/file_extensions.py (EXTENSION_TO_ARRAY).

ARGUMENTS
  Positional string or path= / _path= — directory to load.
  Optional second positional or pattern= — glob filter (e.g. '*.py', '*.wav').
  source_path=False — copy files into the session (default is True: link originals).
  subfolders=True — include files in subdirectories (recursive).

BEHAVIOR
  Resolves the directory relative to cwd, repo root, or session directory.
  By default skips subdirectories; set subfolders=True to walk them.
  File order is sorted by relative path (recursive) or filename (flat).
  By default (source_path=True), arrays hold absolute paths to source files on disk.
  Set source_path=False to copy file contents into the session instead.

  AH_EMULATE_FOLDER=1 — write placeholder links without reading disk (tests).

EXAMPLE
  @videos: $folder('test_data/videos')
  @sources: $folder('src', '*.py')
  @lib: $folder('ahlib', source_path=True)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
